ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2016-07-14T03:56:44Z","label":{"name":"bug","color":"fc2929"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/232552439","html_url":"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/1728#issuecomment-232552439","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/1728","id":232552439,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMjU1MjQzOQ==","user":{"login":"nicoddemus","id":1085180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODUxODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1085180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus","html_url":"https://github.com/nicoddemus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-07-14T04:15:04Z","updated_at":"2016-07-14T04:15:04Z","body":"I see the error happening with `teardown_function()` as you mention, but when I add a `setup_function()` method I get a similar error for the `setup_function()` as well:\n\n``` python\nfrom __future__ import print_function\n\ndef setup_function():\n    print('\\nIn setup_function()')\n\ndef test_something():\n    print('\\nIn test_something()')\n\ndef teardown_function():\n    print('\\nIn teardown_function()')\n```\n\n```\n$ py.test\n> setup_func_or_method(self.obj)\nE TypeError: setup_function() takes 0 positional arguments but 1 was given\n```\n\nAccording to the [docs](http://doc.pytest.org/en/latest/xunit_setup.html), all `setup/teardown` functions and methods receive an argument, so the behavior seems correct to me.\n\nHmm I made some other tests, and it seems there's some inconsistency, because `setup_module` and `teardown_module` can receive or not the `module` argument, while `*_method` and `*_function` must always receive it.\n\nSo it seems the problem is actually that `*_module` and `*_function/*_method` behave differently: the former can receive or not an object, while the latter ones must always receive an object.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/232552439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nicoddemus","id":1085180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODUxODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1085180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus","html_url":"https://github.com/nicoddemus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/232552886","html_url":"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/1728#issuecomment-232552886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/1728","id":232552886,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMjU1Mjg4Ng==","user":{"login":"nicoddemus","id":1085180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODUxODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1085180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus","html_url":"https://github.com/nicoddemus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-07-14T04:19:08Z","updated_at":"2016-07-14T04:19:20Z","body":"Digging a little further, it is clear why this is inconsistent: `Module` explicitly handles the optional argument:\n\n``` python\n        if setup_module is not None:\n            #XXX: nose compat hack, move to nose plugin\n            # if it takes a positional arg, its probably a pytest style one\n            # so we pass the current module object\n            if _has_positional_arg(setup_module):\n                setup_module(self.obj)\n            else:\n                setup_module()\n```\n\n(similar code for `teardown_module`)\n\nIMO the correct solution is to apply the same handling for `*_method` and `*_function` forms to keep consistency (the other way around would break backward compatibility).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/232552886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nicoddemus","id":1085180,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwODUxODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1085180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus","html_url":"https://github.com/nicoddemus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nicoddemus/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/comments/232559906","html_url":"https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/1728#issuecomment-232559906","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pytest-dev/pytest/issues/1728","id":232559906,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzMjU1OTkwNg==","user":{"login":"okken","id":1568356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjgzNTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1568356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/okken","html_url":"https://github.com/okken","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okken/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/okken/foll